\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The paper in one figure.} \textbf  {(A)} Against blind human soundness grades, all five reference-comparison metrics land within noise of zero, while verification-shaped signals carry real signal, topping out at the prefix-repair curve ($+0.79$, measured on labeling round two; other entries on round one, Section~\ref {sec:setup}). \textbf  {(B)} The mechanism: across 6{,}000 model--item pairs, teacher-forced accuracy is $80\%$ reference perplexity. It measures the reference, not the solution. \textbf  {(C)} Under best-of-64 selection pressure (25 configurations, two domains), blind and sabotaged judges (orange) are hacked, with high scoreboard inflation, high accuracy loss, or both, while referenced judges (blue) resist. The two labeled exceptions are the paper's two mechanisms: the 1.5B code judge that cannot \emph  {use} its reference (the capability gate), and the sabotaged frontier judge that deceives the metric without damaging selection.}}{3}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:master}{{2}{3}{\textbf {The paper in one figure.} \textbf {(A)} Against blind human soundness grades, all five reference-comparison metrics land within noise of zero, while verification-shaped signals carry real signal, topping out at the prefix-repair curve ($+0.79$, measured on labeling round two; other entries on round one, Section~\ref {sec:setup}). \textbf {(B)} The mechanism: across 6{,}000 model--item pairs, teacher-forced accuracy is $80\%$ reference perplexity. It measures the reference, not the solution. \textbf {(C)} Under best-of-64 selection pressure (25 configurations, two domains), blind and sabotaged judges (orange) are hacked, with high scoreboard inflation, high accuracy loss, or both, while referenced judges (blue) resist. The two labeled exceptions are the paper's two mechanisms: the 1.5B code judge that cannot \emph {use} its reference (the capability gate), and the sabotaged frontier judge that deceives the metric without damaging selection}{figure.caption.2}{}}
